[2] BY HAND, before code: the general-order eps-matching.
    Rather than doing the eps^3 order as a one-off, I carried the matching at
    a symbolic order index p, because the shift s = (1-t) + eps is exact and
    every Taylor expansion involved terminates.  Result (my own derivation,
    written down before any script existed):

      t (Phi[p])' + (1+r+b) Phi[p]
        = [p==0]
        + r     sum_{i=0..p}    (-1)^i/i!     (eta[p-i]_{r-1})^(i)
        + t     sum_{i=2..p+1}  (-1)^i/i!     (Phi[p+1-i]_r)^(i)
        + (1+r+b) sum_{i=1..p}  (-1)^(i+1)/i! (Phi[p-i]_r)^(i)

      eta[p]_r(t,b) = [p==1] + r eta[p-1]_{r-1}(t,b+1)
                       + t Phi[p]_r(t,b+1) - (1+b+r) Phi[p-1]_r(t,b+1)

    Checked by hand that p=0 reproduces Fact 2, p=1 reproduces Fact 3, and
    p=2 reproduces Estagio 8's boxed H_r ODE and L_r relation
    character-for-character (it does; see ATTEMPT.md Sec.2.3).  The p=3
    instance is the mandated (I_r, M_r) pair.

