[8] SELF-CAUGHT ISSUES
    - First draft of the order-p ODE had the sign of the eta-derivative terms
      wrong (I wrote (+1)^i/i! from the forward shift, forgetting that
      d/ds = -d/dt under s = 1-t).  Caught by checking that p=1 must reproduce
      Fact 3, which it did not until the sign was fixed.  Corrected before any
      code was written; the corrected form is what appears in [2] above.
    - The b>=1 closed form for D*^(p)_r(b) was attempted in the same
      {r^q varphi_r} + {r^q} basis and FAILS out of sample (54-56 failures out
      of 61).  Reported as OPEN, not forced.  This is the same phenomenon the
      predecessor reported for its own order-2 constant at b>=1.
    - The order-3,4,5 closed forms of D*^(p)_r(0) are FITS, verified far out
      of sample but not proved.  Labelled NUMERICALLY VERIFIED, not PROVED.

